From a3caf053629f2d549946bd8764316a8af8d6ee36 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rolotrealanis98 <122947376+rolotrealanis98@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 20:58:47 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 30/33] arm64: dts: apple: t6050: mark the boot framebuffer as
 the built-in panel

Both T6050 laptops (J714s, J716s) hand the internal panel over as the
m1n1 framebuffer. Mark framebuffer0 "apple,internal-panel" so simpledrm
registers an eDP connector (previous patch), which is what makes Omarchy
lock on lid close and lay its bar out around the notch.

The power-domains the J714c tree also adds (ps_disp_cpu) are left out:
our framebuffer node has none today and the domain's behaviour on J716s
is not measured.

Based on edimoldovan/linux-aurora 9dee12b1266c (t6050-j714c.dts hunk).

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-jxxx.dtsi | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-jxxx.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-jxxx.dtsi
index 3440b6202..c64f42c03 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-jxxx.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-jxxx.dtsi
@@ -28,6 +28,8 @@ framebuffer0: framebuffer@0 {
 			 * t6050 pmgr domain offsets are known */
 			/* Format properties will be added by loader */
 			status = "disabled";
+			/* The built-in panel: simpledrm reports it as eDP */
+			apple,internal-panel;
 		};
 	};
 
